          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Grass-fed whey is a farming-practice choice, not a performance upgrade. The protein is the same, and the grass-fed fat advantage barely survives the filtering. What you are paying for is pasture-based dairy, no added growth hormones and, often, a shorter label, and those are fair things to pay a little more for if they matter to you.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most buyers, Transparent Labs is the best grass-fed isolate and Naked Whey the best-value concentrate, both under about $2 per 25 g of protein. Choose Legion if you want a named, audited standard, Momentous if you are drug-tested, and Truvani if you want organic too. Whatever you pick, ask which standard backs the claim, and do the cost-per-25 g sum before you check out.
